I've written two task files and the issue-responses file for this session. The commit didn't go through because session_plan/ is in .gitignore; the plan command ends with || true, so the files are on disk but not committed.

Task 1 (product): Fixes #1242. `/doctor` gets an API row. I filed #1242 during planning for the biggest gap the assessment found. /doctor checks that an API key exists but never whether the provider actually answers. Claude Code 2.1.331 added a row for this.
• The check sends one minimal request through the same model setup a real run uses, so the key only goes where a run would send it. It has a time limit.
• The result is one of: reached, key rejected, model or endpoint not found, can't reach the host, timed out, or skipped because there's no key.
• All the new code goes in a new file, src/doctor_api.rs. src/commands_dev.rs is at 1975 lines with no size-limit entry, so it only gets the call.
• The check is wired where the doctor command runs, not inside run_doctor_checks, because existing tests call that function directly and must not start going to the network.
• Tests run only against a local fake server, never a real provider. They include a deliberate break-and-restore run to show the tests can fail.

Task 2 (product): Fixes #1208. This uses the backlog-drain slot (17 open self-filed issues; #1208 has the least work left).
• Gemini 3.6+: Google's docs say these models silently ignore temperature. yoyo will mark those models so its existing "temperature dropped" note prints, with Google's reason, and I'll ask yoagent upstream to add the same rule.
• The other two rows (OpenAI-compatible servers on another host, and OpenRouter's 1.0 cap) each get a decision taken from the docs of vLLM, llama.cpp and OpenRouter. No calls are made with a real key.

